{%- comment -%}
  Product card — the photograph.

  Every photograph the piece has is a slide, however many that is, and only the
  first two are fetched up front. That is `snippets/card-slide.liquid`'s rule
  and the reason a slide is `opacity: 0` rather than `display: none`; see
  "Product card" in CLAUDE.md before changing anything here.

  The arrows and the badge stay **inside** this block rather than becoming
  blocks of their own, and that is structural rather than a judgement about how
  much a merchant should be able to remove: `.card__arrow` is
  `position: absolute; top: 50%`, so its containing block has to be
  `.card__media`. Lifted out to be a sibling it would centre itself on the whole
  card — the caption included — and sit over the price.

  **Every setting the photograph obeys is this block's own.** There is no
  "Product cards" group in the theme settings any more; a card is edited where
  the card is. `snippets/product-card.liquid` still draws the collection and
  search grids and now carries its own defaults, so those two grids are fixed
  until they are rebuilt on blocks — which is the honest state of a theme that
  has one card built two ways.

  **Nothing here knows what the shop sells.** The framing correction used to be
  a table matching "bracelet", "earring" and "ring" against the product's type
  and title, with a `custom.card_zoom` metafield in front of it — one
  catalogue's categories and one shop's metafield, both written into the theme.
  It is a single setting now, and because it is a text setting it takes a
  dynamic source: bind it to whatever metafield a shop keeps and every piece
  gets its own figure; type one and the whole row shares it; leave it and there
  is no correction at all.

  The order of the slides is the product's own. The option control deliberately
  does not touch it: "Colour is chosen on the card itself: the name, the price
  and what goes in the bag all follow it. The photograph does not."
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign product = closest.product

  assign img_loading = 'lazy'
  assign img_sizes = '(max-width: 700px) 70vw, 460px'

  comment
    Every value has to do what it says, `adapt` included — it fell through to
    the same 3/4 box once, so choosing it changed nothing at all. Adapt takes
    the shape from the first photograph the card actually shows; a card with no
    photograph keeps 3/4, there being nothing to adapt to.
  endcomment
  assign ratio_setting = block.settings.image_ratio

  assign ratio_value = '3 / 4'
  if ratio_setting == 'adapt'
    assign ratio_media = product.media | where: 'media_type', 'image' | first
    if ratio_media.width > 0 and ratio_media.height > 0
      assign ratio_value = ratio_media.width | append: ' / ' | append: ratio_media.height
    endif
  else
    assign ratio_value = ratio_setting | replace: '/', ' / '
  endif

  assign fit_value = block.settings.image_fit

  comment
    The framing correction, as a number the merchant supplies rather than a
    category the theme recognises. Coerced and tested rather than printed
    blindly: a dynamic source bound to a metafield one product is missing
    returns nothing, and `--card-zoom: 0` would collapse the photograph to a
    point. Anything that is not a positive number simply means no correction.
  endcomment
  assign card_zoom = blank
  assign zoom_number = block.settings.zoom | plus: 0
  if zoom_number > 0
    assign card_zoom = zoom_number
  endif

  assign card_images = product.media | where: 'media_type', 'image'
  assign photo_count = card_images.size

  comment
    The video counts only once an mp4 rendition is known to exist. Counting the
    media itself put the arrows and the badge on a card whose video has none —
    controls for a slide that is never rendered, because the slide is guarded
    on the rendition and the count was not.
  endcomment
  assign card_video = blank
  assign card_mp4 = blank
  if block.settings.show_video
    assign product_videos = product.media | where: 'media_type', 'video'
    assign first_video = product_videos.first
    if first_video != blank
      assign mp4_sources = first_video.sources | where: 'format', 'mp4'
      assign card_mp4 = mp4_sources.last
      if card_mp4 != blank
        assign card_video = first_video
      endif
    endif
  endif

  assign slide_count = photo_count
  if card_video != blank
    assign slide_count = slide_count | plus: 1
  endif

  comment
    The badge is the merchant's word. The design's is "360°", which is true of
    its own footage and of nothing else — a shop whose video is a model wearing
    the piece should not have a chip claiming a spin.
  endcomment
  assign video_label = block.settings.video_badge
  if video_label == blank
    assign video_label = 'products.video_view' | t
  endif

  comment
    Slide 0 is what the card shows and slide 1 is what hover previews. Those
    two are the whole of it without scripting, so those two are what the
    browser fetches.
  endcomment
  assign eager_slides = 2
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  `data-hover-off` turns off the preview-the-next-photograph behaviour, and it
  has to sit here rather than on the card root because it is this block's
  setting — a block cannot write an attribute onto its parent. Both the
  stylesheet's no-JavaScript swap and `theme.js`'s own hover state test for it
  on `.card__media`.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="card__media"
  style="aspect-ratio: {{ ratio_value }};{% if card_zoom != blank %} --card-zoom: {{ card_zoom }};{% endif %} --card-fit: {{ fit_value }};"
  {% unless block.settings.hover_next %}data-hover-off{% endunless %}
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  {%- if product == blank -%}
    {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder-svg' }}
  {%- elsif slide_count > 0 -%}
    {%- assign slide_i = 0 -%}

    {%- for media in card_images -%}
      {%- assign slide_eager = false -%}
      {%- if slide_i < eager_slides -%}
        {%- assign slide_eager = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {% render 'card-slide',
        media: media,
        index: slide_i,
        eager: slide_eager,
        product: product,
        sizes: img_sizes,
        loading: img_loading
      %}
      {%- assign slide_i = slide_i | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- endfor -%}

    {%- if card_video != blank -%}
      {%- assign card_video_lqip = card_video.preview_image | image_url: width: 40 -%}
      <span
        class="card__slide{% if photo_count == 0 %} is-on{% endif %}"
        data-card-slide="{{ photo_count }}"
        data-card-spin
      >
        <video
          class="card__img card__video"
          data-src="{{ card_mp4.url }}"
          poster="{{ card_video.preview_image | image_url: width: 600 }}"
          width="{{ card_video.preview_image.width | default: 1240 }}"
          height="{{ card_video.preview_image.height | default: 827 }}"
          muted
          loop
          playsinline
          preload="none"
          aria-label="{{ video_label | escape }}"
          data-video-lqip="{{ card_video_lqip }}"
        ></video>
        {% render 'video-lqip-frame', lqip: card_video_lqip %}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    <span class="card__slide is-on">
      {{ 'product-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder-svg' }}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if card_video != blank -%}
    <span class="card__spin" data-card-spin-label{% if photo_count > 0 %} hidden{% endif %}>
      {{- video_label -}}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if block.settings.show_arrows and slide_count > 1 -%}
    <button
      class="card__arrow card__arrow--prev"
      type="button"
      data-card-step="-1"
      data-tip="{{ 'products.previous_view' | t }}"
      aria-label="{{ 'products.previous_view' | t }}"
    >
      <svg width="10" height="20" viewBox="0 0 12 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M10 2L2 12l8 10" />
      </svg>
    </button>
    <button
      class="card__arrow card__arrow--next"
      type="button"
      data-card-step="1"
      data-tip="{{ 'products.next_view' | t }}"
      aria-label="{{ 'products.next_view' | t }}"
    >
      <svg width="10" height="20" viewBox="0 0 12 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M2 2l8 10-8 10" />
      </svg>
    </button>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if product != blank -%}
    {%- if product.available == false -%}
      <span class="badge">{{ 'products.sold_out' | t }}</span>
    {%- elsif product.compare_at_price > product.price -%}
      <span class="badge">{{ 'products.on_sale' | t }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:blocks.product_card_image.name",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_ratio",
      "label": "t:sections.all.image_ratio.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "adapt", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.adapt" },
        { "value": "1/1", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.square" },
        { "value": "4/5", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.portrait" },
        { "value": "3/4", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.tall_portrait" },
        { "value": "4/3", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.landscape" }
      ],
      "default": "1/1"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_fit",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_image.image_fit.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_image.image_fit.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "contain", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.contain" },
        { "value": "cover", "label": "t:settings_schema.options.cover" }
      ],
      "default": "contain"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "zoom",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_image.zoom.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_image.zoom.info"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "t:blocks.product_card_image.views_header"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "hover_next",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_image.hover_next.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_image.hover_next.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_arrows",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_image.show_arrows.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_image.show_arrows.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_video",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_image.show_video.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_image.show_video.info",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "video_badge",
      "label": "t:blocks.product_card_image.video_badge.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.product_card_image.video_badge.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ block.settings.show_video }}",
      "default": "Video"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "t:blocks.product_card_image.name"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
